{
  "id": "Compound::DB08933 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Luliconazole is likely to influence Cyp3a4 through a series of metabolic pathways involving Cyp2c19. The evidence suggests that Luliconazole binds to Cyp2c19, which then participates in metabolic processes such as monoterpenoid metabolism or steroid hydroxylase activity. These processes are ultimately linked to Cyp3a4, indicating that Luliconazole may modulate Cyp3a4 activity indirectly through Cyp2c19. The overlapping pathways highlight a potential mechanism where Luliconazole affects Cyp3a4 by influencing the expression or activity of Cyp2c19, which in turn impacts the metabolic capacity of Cyp3a4. The consistent binding to Cyp2c19 across all three paths supports a central role for this enzyme in the metabolic cascade leading to Cyp3a4 involvement.",
